  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "lem:geometric-mixing-anchor-moment",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Suppose \\(0<\\lambda\\le1\\), the kernel is bounded and continuous and is bounded away from zero on a ball about the origin, and \\(c_G\\) satisfies the stated population-Gram compatibility bound. Under \\texttt{ass:design-density} and \\texttt{ass:temporal-mixing}, for each fixed cohort and interior \\(z_0\\),\n\\[\n\\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal M_{N,T,\\mathbf n}}\\mathbb E_P[(h_s^\\star)^{2\\lambda}\\mid z_0]\n\\le C\\left\\{(Tn_s)^{-2\\lambda/(2\\lambda+d)}+N^{-\\lambda}+\\left(\\frac{\\log(T\\vee2)}{T}\\right)^{2\\lambda/d}\\right\\}.\n\\]\nThe same assertion with exponent \\(\\lambda\\) holds after taking square roots. Moreover, \\(\\sup_P\\Pr_P(\\mathsf F_{\\mathrm{fb}}\\mid z_0)\\le CT^{-2}\\). On the independent-calendar subclass, the logarithmic spacing term is replaced by \\(T^{-2\\lambda/d}\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "lambda",
      "K",
      "c_G",
      "c_X",
      "beta_0",
      "rho_0",
      "M",
      "N",
      "T",
      "n_s",
      "n_vec",
      "s",
      "z_0",
      "h_s_star",
      "F_fb",
      "C"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:panel-model-class",
      "def:realized-geometry",
      "def:conditional-rate",
      "def:frontier-estimator",
      "ass:interior-path",
